# The Dark Knight's first job node and the hardest-hitting single cast in the
# game: nine spears of seven lines each, 55,125% at master. GMS's own numbers,
# and against every Explorer V node in the client only a 6th job skill throws
# more per second. It roughly doubles the class's sustained damage.
#
# Nine casts rather than 63 lines, for the same reason Sword Illusion is twelve
# and five: the ledger draws what GMS draws, and each spear rolls its own
# mastery and criticals.
#
# The 660ms cast is FIXED. Every one of the six animation frames carries a
# negative delay -- the client's mark for a frame attack speed does not
# shorten -- where Dark Impale's is -180 then four scaled frames. So a Dark
# Knight at the speed cap swings Dark Impale in 510ms and still stands still
# for the whole 660 here.
#
# Dropped: the up-and-down aiming, which needs a screen this game does not
# draw; immunity to attack reflection, which nothing inflicts; and the 10% cut
# to %HP-ratio damage taken during the wind-up.
name: "Spear of Darkness"
description: "Hurls a spear of utter darkness at the enemy."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_DARK_KNIGHT_V skill_order: 1 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_SPEAR
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_POLEARM
base_delay_ms: 660
fixed_delay: true
cooldown_seconds: 10.0
max_enemies: 12
lines: 7
casts: 9
base {
  skill_pct: 4.11
  crit_rate: 1.00
  ied_pct: 0.50
}
per_level { skill_pct: 0.16 }
